    {
      "type": "card",
      "text": "Because she reaches so far, the queen can attack two things at once, as here. By convention she is worth about nine pawns, more than a rook (five). [I] Practical advice that follows, our inference rather than a measured rule: do not trade her carelessly, and be wary of bringing her out early where smaller pieces can chase her."
    },
    {
      "type": "card",
      "text": "**Rule of thumb, for tapping squares.** Take one of her eight lines at a time. Walk away from her square one step at a time. Stop before your own piece. Stop on the first enemy piece, counting that square. Stop at the edge. Then move to the next line, and finish all eight before you tap."
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "item": "IBG-LFNDQUEENKING1-5"
    },
